  "findings": [
    {
      "area": "binding and lifetime",
      "result": "PASS",
      "evidence": "7 fixed slices of 2305 bytes; 2304 wire bytes plus private NUL each. Caller-owned block bound once under stats mux, no hot allocation, fallback, runtime free or rebinding. Same-address PoolInit leaves live generation/owned slots unchanged; different address rejected. Only an unpublished failed-binding allocation can be freed."
    },
    {
      "area": "ownership and payload consumers",
      "result": "PASS",
      "evidence": "Allocation/release and generation checks remain locked; memcpy/parse stay outside lock while producer owns descriptor. Consumer and supersede paths obtain ownership from queue before release. BLE/Wi-Fi publication APIs deep-copy before returning; no DMA/ISR queue metadata moved to PSRAM. Capacity unchanged: 4 ordinary, 1 lifecycle, 2 protected."
    },
    {
      "area": "init and failure",
      "result": "PASS",
      "evidence": "Overall init claim rejects concurrent entry before a second allocation/task creation. Partial task creation retry preserves queues and existing task handles; completed init retains network/storage errors, optional Serial binding alone retryable. Sticky PSRAM failure still creates transport/control tasks and queues; actual Queue regression returns NO_MEM without NULL copy. This is scoped Init serialization, not a claim that all runtime calls are globally thread-safe."
    },
    {
      "area": "metadata and identity",
      "result": "PASS",
      "evidence": "Three NULL guards only; 66896 legacy metadata comparisons and 20 true-encoder CRC cases unchanged. 96 real typed-encoder cases retain original bytes, identities and SHORT/full behavior; 1040 legacy conversions still avoided."
    },
    {
      "area": "NVS and calibration",
      "result": "PASS",
      "evidence": "Both init autoerase branches removed. Calibration init errors short-circuit load/query/save before open/write/commit; 3 errors \u00d7 4 APIs preserved saved bytes and later valid reload. Generic NVS failure remains visible on repeated Init while independent control starts. No physical NVS fault injection."
    },
    {
      "area": "MEM",
      "result": "PASS",
      "evidence": "Read-only sequential heap snapshots, no heap traversal/formatting under memory mux; transport diagnostic copy acquires its own mux after memory mux release. New pool readiness/error/internal/external fields do not redefine old owned-memory totals. Maximum response 394 bytes including newline, 395 with NUL, capacity 512."
    }
  ],
